# Azure API Management (APIM) & Application Gateway Rules

## APIM — API Design Rules
- Register every Express service API in APIM; never expose Express directly to the internet.
- Use **OpenAPI 3.0 spec** as the source of truth; import into APIM from spec file.
- Version APIs in the URL path: `/api/v1/`, `/api/v2/`.
- Group related operations under a single APIM **API**; use **Products** for access tiers.

## APIM Policy Rules
- Apply policies at the **global** → **product** → **API** → **operation** hierarchy (most broad to most specific).
- Mandatory global policies:

```xml
<!-- inbound -->
<cors allow-credentials="true">
  <allowed-origins><origin>https://yourdomain.com</origin></allowed-origins>
  <allowed-methods><method>GET</method><method>POST</method><method>PUT</method><method>DELETE</method></allowed-methods>
  <allowed-headers><header>Authorization</header><header>Content-Type</header></allowed-headers>
</cors>
<rate-limit-by-key calls="1000" renewal-period="60"
  counter-key="@(context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("X-Forwarded-For",""))" />
<set-header name="X-Request-Id" exists-action="skip">
  <value>@(Guid.NewGuid().ToString())</value>
</set-header>

<!-- backend -->
<set-backend-service base-url="{{BackendBaseUrl}}" />
<forward-request timeout="30" />

<!-- outbound -->
<set-header name="X-Content-Type-Options" exists-action="override"><value>nosniff</value></set-header>
<set-header name="X-Frame-Options" exists-action="override"><value>DENY</value></set-header>
```

## Authentication & Authorization in APIM
- Validate **JWT tokens** in APIM inbound policy; don't validate again in Express (trust APIM).
- Use `validate-jwt` policy with Azure AD / Entra ID JWKS endpoint.

```xml
<validate-jwt header-name="Authorization" failed-validation-httpcode="401" failed-validation-error-message="Unauthorized">
  <openid-config url="https://login.microsoftonline.com/{tenant-id}/v2.0/.well-known/openid-configuration" />
  <required-claims>
    <claim name="aud"><value>api://{client-id}</value></claim>
  </required-claims>
</validate-jwt>
```

## Backend Health & Circuit Breaker
- Configure APIM **backends** with health probes.
- Use the `retry` policy for transient failures (max 3 retries, exponential backoff).

```xml
<retry condition="@(context.Response.StatusCode >= 500)" count="3" interval="2" delta="1" max-interval="10">
  <forward-request />
</retry>
```

## Subscription Keys
- Require subscription keys for all APIs except health-check endpoints.
- Scope keys to **Products** (not individual APIs).
- Rotate keys via APIM Named Values; never hardcode in backend.

## Named Values (Secrets)
- Store all backend URLs, secrets, and feature flags as **Named Values** in APIM.
- Use `{{BackendBaseUrl}}`, `{{JwtSecret}}` syntax in policies.
- Link Named Values to **Azure Key Vault** for secrets.

---

## Application Gateway Rules
- Place Application Gateway **in front of APIM** for WAF protection.
- Enable **WAF v2** in Prevention mode with OWASP 3.2 rule set.
- Configure APIM as the **backend pool** target (private IP or internal APIM URL).
- Enable **end-to-end TLS** (HTTPS from client → AppGW → APIM → Express).
- Terminate SSL at AppGW with managed certificate (Azure-issued).

## AppGW Health Probes
- Configure custom health probes per backend (path: `/health`, interval: 30s, threshold: 2).
- APIM's built-in health endpoint: `GET /status-0123456789abcdef`.

## Express Backend — Rules When Behind APIM/AppGW
- Trust the proxy: add `app.set('trust proxy', 1)` in Express.
- Use `X-Forwarded-For` for real client IP (set by AppGW).
- Validate `X-Request-Id` header forwarded by APIM; include in all log entries.
- Health endpoint must be **unauthenticated** and respond within 200ms.

```js
// src/routes/health-routes.js
import { Router } from 'express';
const router = Router();

router.get('/health', async (req, res) => {
  res.json({ status: 'ok', timestamp: new Date().toISOString() });
});

router.get('/health/ready', async (req, res) => {
  // Check DB connections
  try {
    await mysqlPool.query('SELECT 1');
    await mongoose.connection.db.command({ ping: 1 });
    res.json({ status: 'ready' });
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(503).json({ status: 'unavailable', error: err.message });
  }
});

export default router;
```

## Observability
- Pass `X-Request-Id` (set by APIM) through to all downstream service calls and DB queries.
- Emit `X-Correlation-Id` in responses for client-side tracing.
- Stream APIM diagnostic logs to **Azure Monitor / Application Insights**.
- Tag all APIM APIs with `environment`, `team`, `service` tags for cost attribution.
